		<p class="eyebrow">Read the evidence behind the playbook</p>
		<h1>Primary sources for practical decisions.</h1>
		<p class="lede">Bait Bikes distinguishes documented cases and practitioner guidance from universal claims. Start here, then apply local law, local data, community review, and your own evaluation.</p>
	</header>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Bicycle theft and bait operations</p><h2>Problem analysis and public-agency experience.</h2></div><p>The strongest general lesson is to analyze the local problem and combine enforcement with prevention. Existing bait-bike evidence includes operational reports and anecdotal findings; local programs should measure their own impact.</p></div>
			<div class="resource-list">
				<a class="resource" href="https://portal.cops.usdoj.gov/resourcecenter/content.ashx/cops-p141-pub.pdf"><span>U.S. DOJ · COPS Office</span><p><strong>Bicycle Theft problem-oriented policing guide.</strong> Theft methods, analysis questions, prevention, markets, registration, and tracker-equipped bait-bike programs.</p><b>Open ↗</b></a>
				<a class="resource" href="https://www.ojp.gov/library/publications/baiting-bicycle-thief"><span>U.S. DOJ · OJP</span><p><strong>Baiting a Bicycle Thief.</strong> Summary of a UCSB Police Department GPS bait-bike program used to learn when and where theft occurred.</p><b>Open ↗</b></a>
				<a class="resource" href="https://www.bart.gov/news/articles/2014/news20140502"><span>BART</span><p><strong>Joint bait-bike operation.</strong> A public-agency account involving two arrests, a repeat offender, and recovery of a separately reported stolen bicycle.</p><b>Open ↗</b></a>
				<a class="resource" href="https://www.ojp.gov/library/publications/bait-vehicle-technologies-and-motor-vehicle-theft-along-southwest-border"><span>U.S. DOJ · OJP</span><p><strong>Bait-vehicle technologies.</strong> Practitioner discussion of tracking, communications, mapping, control, recording, and operational analysis for bait cars.</p><b>Open ↗</b></a>
